      "url": "https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/cisa-flags-sonicwall-sonicos-mfa-bypass.html",
      "title": "CISA flags SonicWall firewall flaw that can bypass MFA",
      "content_html": "The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency added a high-severity SonicWall SonicOS SSL-VPN flaw to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog on Nov. 9, citing evidence of active exploitation. SonicWall said it had investigated a report of possible attacks. The flaw, CVE-2026-19868, can allow attackers with valid credentials for an alternate authentication method to bypass Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML) controls and any multifactor authentication (MFA) enforced through SAML. It affects only configurations with SAML enabled for SSL-VPN logins.\n\nSonicWall urged customers to install its updated firmware. U.S. civilian federal agencies must apply the fix by Nov. 20, 2026. The company has not disclosed details of the suspected attacks, and neither SonicWall nor CISA has published indicators of compromise.",
