      "title": "Tesla to end Cybertruck production by mid-2027, shift factory to robotaxi production",
      "content_html": "Tesla will wind down Cybertruck production at its Texas factory by mid-2027 and redirect capacity to its Cybercab robotaxi, CEO Elon Musk said. Musk said Nov. 9 that Tesla would add a production shift and build as many trucks as possible before closing the line in about eight months, then refund deposits to many customers whose orders it cannot fill.\n\nMusk said orders exceed production and that Tesla is not dropping the truck for lack of profitability. Its manufacturing complexity, he said, makes additional Cybercab production a better use of resources. U.S. Cybertruck sales fell 48% to 20,237 in 2025, according to Kelley Blue Book. Cox Automotive estimated sales of 11,586 in the first nine months of 2026, down 28% year over year. Musk had previously projected annual sales of 250,000.\n\nCybercab began commercial deployment in an Austin robotaxi pilot in September, and the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration opened a probe into how Tesla certified about 1,000 vehicles as meeting federal safety standards. Tesla has not specified how many customers will receive refunds.",
