      "url": "https://sourcenm.com/2026/11/09/us-senate-advances-new-mexico-us-sen-heinrichs-controversial-permit-reform-bill/",
      "title": "Senate advances energy permitting bill as Trump rejects wind turbines",
      "content_html": "The U.S. Senate voted 73-25 on Monday to begin debate on a bipartisan bill that would speed up federal permitting for energy and infrastructure projects, including power plants, transmission lines and data centers. The vote cleared a procedural hurdle, not final passage, allowing floor debate and amendments. Known as the Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act, the bill would also require large data-center operators to cover more of the cost of grid upgrades their facilities require.\n\nThe measure has split Democrats. Some argue that amendments released over the weekend address tribal consultation and community concerns, while critics say environmental safeguards and tribal authority remain at risk. The bill’s sponsors say it can lower power costs and accelerate clean-energy construction; opponents want Congress to wait until Democrats take control of both chambers in January.\n\nPresident Donald Trump backed the bill but said Monday he would not approve wind turbines, while Democratic supporters expect the legislation to help renewable projects. Senators are expected to debate amendments and hold a final vote in the coming days. If approved, the bill would still need House passage before reaching Trump.",
