      "id": "https://thenextweb.com/news/ibm-concert-protect-claude-mythos-vulnerability-scanning",
      "url": "https://thenextweb.com/news/ibm-concert-protect-claude-mythos-vulnerability-scanning",
      "title": "Cisco and IBM plan to add Anthropic’s Mythos to security tools",
      "content_html": "Cisco and IBM plan to add Anthropic’s Claude Mythos, a restricted AI model used for cybersecurity reasoning, to enterprise security products that test AI systems or scan software for vulnerabilities. Cisco plans to make Mythos available soon to selected enterprise customers through its AI Defense red-teaming service; IBM plans to integrate it into Concert Protect, with general availability in early 2027.\n\nThe companies will offer Mythos through controlled product workflows rather than give customers open access to the model. Cisco says tests will be limited to registered, authorized targets and tied to named operators, with controls to stop sessions and record actions. IBM’s planned workflow will use Mythos to find weaknesses, assess whether they can be exploited in a customer’s environment, and propose fixes for developers to review and approve.",
